### # 1. A Ground-Mat for Harvesting Resin
<a id="term-1-a-ground-mat-for-harvesting-resin"></a>

Overview: [back to tools.md](./tools.md#term-1-a-ground-mat-for-harvesting-resin)

Meaning: In the harvesting of myrrh (*smyrna*), *psiathoi* are spread out on the ground beneath the myrrh tree.

#### Default sense
<a id="sense-1-a-ground-mat-for-harvesting-resin-sense-1"></a>

Relevance: `non_perfume`

In the harvesting of myrrh (*smyrna*), *psiathoi* are spread out on the ground beneath the myrrh tree.

##### Dioscorides, *De materia medica* (Book 1, chapter 64, section 1) *(Also repeated closely by Oribasius, Collectiones medicae, Book 12).*
<a id="cit-1-a-ground-mat-for-harvesting-resin-cit-1"></a>

Source class: `primary_technical`
Usage type: `recipe`

**Greek**

> "...οὗ ἐγκοπτομένου ἀπορρεῖ τὸ δάκρυον εἰς ὑπεστρωμένας ψιάθους, τὸ δὲ τῷ στελέχει περιπήγνυται."

**Translation**

> "...from which, when it is cut, the tear [resin] flows down onto rush mats (*psiathous*) spread underneath, while some congeals around the trunk."

Reference: Dioscorides, *De materia medica* (Book 1, chapter 64, section 1) *(Also repeated closely by Oribasius, Collectiones medicae, Book 12).*

Context note: In the harvesting of myrrh (*smyrna*), *psiathoi* are spread out on the ground beneath the myrrh tree.

