### # 3. The Floor of the Nasal Cavity (Anatomical Metaphor)
<a id="term-3-the-floor-of-the-nasal-cavity-anatomical-metaphor"></a>

Overview: [back to tools.md](./tools.md#term-3-the-floor-of-the-nasal-cavity-anatomical-metaphor)

Meaning: Because a *lenos* is a trough-like structure, poets and medical writers also applied the term to the hollow troughs or "floors" of the nasal cavities.

#### Default sense
<a id="sense-3-the-floor-of-the-nasal-cavity-anatomical-metaphor-sense-1"></a>

Relevance: `non_perfume`

Because a *lenos* is a trough-like structure, poets and medical writers also applied the term to the hollow troughs or "floors" of the nasal cavities.

##### Theophilus Protospatharius, *De corporis humani fabrica* (Book 4, section 13)
<a id="cit-3-the-floor-of-the-nasal-cavity-anatomical-metaphor-cit-1"></a>

Source class: `appendix_context`
Usage type: `unknown`

**Greek**

> "...τὰ δὲ ἐδάφη τῶν κοιλωμάτων παρὰ τοῖς ποιηταῖς ὀνομάζονται ληνοὶ, τὰ δὲ ἑκατέρωθεν μέρη τοῦ χόνδρου τῆς ῥινὸς πτερύγια."

**Translation**

> "...and the floors of the cavities [of the nose] are named troughs (*lenoi*) by the poets, and the parts on either side of the cartilage of the nose [are called] wings."

Reference: Theophilus Protospatharius, *De corporis humani fabrica* (Book 4, section 13)

Context note: Because a *lenos* is a trough-like structure, poets and medical writers also applied the term to the hollow troughs or "floors" of the nasal cavities.

### # 4. A Carved Hollow in Medical Machinery (Mechanical Metaphor)
<a id="term-4-a-carved-hollow-in-medical-machinery-mechanical-metaphor"></a>

Overview: [back to tools.md](./tools.md#term-4-a-carved-hollow-in-medical-machinery-mechanical-metaphor)

Meaning: In the Hippocratic corpus, the word is used to describe a physical, trough-like depression carved into a wooden board.

#### Default sense
<a id="sense-4-a-carved-hollow-in-medical-machinery-mechanical-metaphor-sense-1"></a>

Relevance: `non_perfume`

In the Hippocratic corpus, the word is used to describe a physical, trough-like depression carved into a wooden board.

##### Hippocrates, *Vectiarius* (Section 38)
<a id="cit-4-a-carved-hollow-in-medical-machinery-mechanical-metaphor-cit-1"></a>

Source class: `appendix_context`
Usage type: `unknown`

**Greek**

> "...καταγλύφους δὲ, ὥσπερ ληνοὺς, λείας ἔχειν, τετραδακτύλους εὖρος καὶ βάθος..."

**Translation**

> "...and to have smooth carved-out hollows, like troughs (*lenoi*), four fingers in width and depth..."

Reference: Hippocrates, *Vectiarius* (Section 38)

Context note: In the Hippocratic corpus, the word is used to describe a physical, trough-like depression carved into a wooden board.

### # 4. Galen on a three-day soak in a double perfumer’s vessel
<a id="term-4-galen-on-a-three-day-soak-in-a-double-perfumer-s-vessel"></a>

Overview: [back to tools.md](./tools.md#term-4-galen-on-a-three-day-soak-in-a-double-perfumer-s-vessel)

Meaning: **Greek** > τὰ προειρημένα εἰς παχέα κόπτεται καὶ βρέχεται ἐν ἀγγείῳ διπλῷ μυρεψικῷ ἐπὶ ἡμέρας γʹ.

#### Default sense
<a id="sense-4-galen-on-a-three-day-soak-in-a-double-perfumer-s-vessel-sense-1"></a>

Relevance: `non_perfume`

**Greek** > τὰ προειρημένα εἰς παχέα κόπτεται καὶ βρέχεται ἐν ἀγγείῳ διπλῷ μυρεψικῷ ἐπὶ ἡμέρας γʹ.

##### ** Galenus, *De compositione medicamentorum secundum locos* x, Kühn 13.55.14 ff.
<a id="cit-4-galen-on-a-three-day-soak-in-a-double-perfumer-s-vessel-cit-1"></a>

Source class: `primary_technical`
Usage type: `unknown`

**Greek**

> τὰ προειρημένα εἰς παχέα κόπτεται καὶ βρέχεται ἐν ἀγγείῳ διπλῷ μυρεψικῷ ἐπὶ ἡμέρας γʹ. τῇ δ' ἐπιούσῃ ἕψεται εἰς τὸ τρίτον, ἔπειτα εἰς κυρτίδα βαλόντες ἐκθλίβομεν τὸ ὑγρὸν εἰς ἕτερον ἀγγεῖον μυρεψικὸν, τὰ δὲ ἀφεψημένα ἀποῤῥίπτομεν.

**Translation**

> The ingredients mentioned above are cut into coarse pieces and soaked in a double perfumer’s vessel for three days. On the following day it is boiled down to a third; then, after putting it into a straining bag, we press the liquid out into another perfumer’s vessel, and the boiled-out solids we throw away.

Reference: ** Galenus, *De compositione medicamentorum secundum locos* x, Kühn 13.55.14 ff.

Context note: **Greek** > τὰ προειρημένα εἰς παχέα κόπτεται καὶ βρέχεται ἐν ἀγγείῳ διπλῷ μυρεψικῷ ἐπὶ ἡμέρας γʹ.

